'''''Medicago intertexta''''', the '''hedgehog medick''',<ref name=BSBI07>{{BSBI 2007 |accessdate=2014-10-17 }}</ref> '''Calvary clover''', or '''Calvary medick''', is a flowering plant of the family ''Fabaceae''. It is found primarily in the western Mediterranean basin. It forms a [[symbiosis|symbiotic]] relationship with the bacterium ''[[Sinorhizobium medicae]]'', which is capable of [[nitrogen fixation]].

A form with red-blotched leaves was formerly much grown as a garden plant.{{Citation needed|date=November 2008}}

